\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Physical PVB continuous frame structure and spectrum. (a) Normalized radial intensity $I(r)/I_{\max }$ for PVBs ($w/R_0 = 0.15$, solid) across $l = 0,2,4,6$ vs.\ $\mathrm  {LG}_{0,l}$ ($w_0 = R_0$, dashed); inset compares the transcendental peak shift $\Delta r/R_0$ ($w/R_0 = 0.25$, circles) with $(l^2/8)(w/R_0)^4$. (b) Normalized radial overlap $\gamma _l(R_0, R_0+\Delta R)$ at $R_0 = 4w$ for $l=0,1,4$ vs.\ $e^{-\Delta R^2/(2w^2)}$ (dotted), marking $13.6\%$ at $2.0w$ and $4.40\%$ at $2.5w$; inset shows azimuthal orthogonality $\delta _{l,l'}$. (c) Spectral multiplier $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle G$}\mathaccent "0365{G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with $\mathcal  {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.39$; inset shows noise gain $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}$ peaking at $(2\sqrt  {\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}})^{-1}$. (d) Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B=1$ and $\kappa (S_w)$ vs.\ $w k_{\max }$, marking the telecom benchmark ($\lambda =1550\,\mathrm  {nm}, \mathrm  {NA}=0.20, w=1.72\,\mu \mathrm  {m}$: $A=0.378, \kappa =2.64$).}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frame_spectrum}{{1}{4}{Physical PVB continuous frame structure and spectrum. (a) Normalized radial intensity $I(r)/I_{\max }$ for PVBs ($w/R_0 = 0.15$, solid) across $l = 0,2,4,6$ vs.\ $\mathrm {LG}_{0,l}$ ($w_0 = R_0$, dashed); inset compares the transcendental peak shift $\Delta r/R_0$ ($w/R_0 = 0.25$, circles) with $(l^2/8)(w/R_0)^4$. (b) Normalized radial overlap $\gamma _l(R_0, R_0+\Delta R)$ at $R_0 = 4w$ for $l=0,1,4$ vs.\ $e^{-\Delta R^2/(2w^2)}$ (dotted), marking $13.6\%$ at $2.0w$ and $4.40\%$ at $2.5w$; inset shows azimuthal orthogonality $\delta _{l,l'}$. (c) Spectral multiplier $\widetilde {G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with $\mathcal {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.39$; inset shows noise gain $\widetilde {H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}$ peaking at $(2\sqrt {\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}})^{-1}$. (d) Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B=1$ and $\kappa (S_w)$ vs.\ $w k_{\max }$, marking the telecom benchmark ($\lambda =1550\,\mathrm {nm}, \mathrm {NA}=0.20, w=1.72\,\mu \mathrm {m}$: $A=0.378, \kappa =2.64$)}{figure.1}{}}
